ing parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(2,1).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}=4p(y-1).\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(4,3),$ so we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=3$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4p(y-1) \\\\ (4-2)^{2} & =4p(3-1) \\\\ 4 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4p(y-1) \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y-1) \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =2(y-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266199 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266200 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266201 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266202 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266203 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1041 "selection" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266200 13194139533925 true] [17592186266198 1110 #uuid "70fe7882-011f-57aa-af16-b57c2078fc13" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266199 1034 "(x+2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}(y+1)" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266199 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533925 true] [17592186266199 1111 #uuid "69727341-5395-5439-876e-81c9187b0654" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266200 1034 "(x-2)^{2}=2(y-1)" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266200 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533925 true] [17592186266200 1111 #uuid "d8394802-2c1c-5dd2-8e17-8223ce180722" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266201 1034 "(x-2)^{2}=4(y-1)" 13194139533925 true] [17592186266201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533925 true] [17592186266201 1111 #uuid "898831f4-09ed-5bbe-a7f1-be49ad5